From 849492f83d94bfb6b5be6ea7483d798dd574a488 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 07:34:04 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 414/417] Translations (ja): a fallback by source text, and the
 words a sweep of every panel found

Dialogs and tool panels stayed in English though the .ts held their
words: PySide's self.tr() asks by class name, and labels made at import
ask before the module's translator is loaded. The last translator asked
now finds a string by its source text alone (fallback_ja.tsv, made from
all the *_ja.ts by make_fallback.py).

The window presets, profile categories, panel presets and the material
parent's None are shown translated (their code keeps the file's name or
the index). Entries marked finished but still English: Base, Body,
Unnamed, World and others; True/False of the gear's fields (by index).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
